1
00:01:57,230 --> 00:01:59,760
Yah! Left high, left low.

2
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:19,540
Right low, lunge right.

3
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:25,430
You break anything, the Septa will have my head.

4
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:26,450
What is...

5
00:02:38,830 --> 00:02:41,390
Your sister knew perfectly well we were to leave today.

6
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:43,610
- How she could forget... - She didn't forget.

7
00:02:43,620 --> 00:02:46,120
She's with her dancing master. She's with him every morning.

8
00:02:46,130 --> 00:02:48,630
She always comes back with scrapes and bruises. She's so clumsy.

9
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:49,660
Hush!

10
00:02:51,490 --> 00:02:52,490
Go back to your room.

11
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:54,960
Bar the doors.

12
00:02:55,340 --> 00:02:57,420
And do not open them for anyone you do not know.

13
00:02:57,430 --> 00:03:00,440
- What is it? What's happening? - Do as I told you.

14
00:03:00,690 --> 00:03:01,490
Run!

15
00:03:05,990 --> 00:03:06,910
This way!

16
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:23,370
Left, right.

17
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:24,950
Now you are dead.

18
00:03:25,510 --> 00:03:26,930
You said right,

19
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:28,880
but you went left.

20
00:03:28,890 --> 00:03:31,290
And now you are a dead girl.

21
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:32,800
Only 'cause you lied.

22
00:03:32,890 --> 00:03:34,000
My tongue lied.

23
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:38,560
My eyes shouted the truth. You were not seeing.

24
00:03:38,570 --> 00:03:40,600
I was so. I watched, but you...

25
00:03:40,610 --> 00:03:44,360
Watching is not seeing, dead girl.

26
00:03:46,450 --> 00:03:49,770
The seeing, the true seeing,

27
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:52,600
that is the heart of swordplay.

28
00:03:57,190 --> 00:03:59,820
Arya Stark, come with us.

29
00:03:59,830 --> 00:04:01,310
Your father wants to see you.

30
00:04:03,310 --> 00:04:07,530
And why is it that Lord Eddard is sending Lannister men

31
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:10,170
in place of his own? I am wondering.

32
00:04:10,180 --> 00:04:12,880
Mind your place, dancing master.

33
00:04:12,890 --> 00:04:15,160
This is no concern of yours.

34
00:04:15,250 --> 00:04:17,470
My father wouldn't send you.

35
00:04:20,700 --> 00:04:23,450
And I don't have to go with you if I don't want.

36
00:04:25,090 --> 00:04:25,920
Take her.

37
00:04:26,130 --> 00:04:29,970
Are you men or snakes, that you would threaten a child?

38
00:04:30,010 --> 00:04:32,210
Get out of my way, little man.

39
00:04:32,630 --> 00:04:35,600
I am Syrio Forel...

40
00:04:35,610 --> 00:04:37,010
Foreign bastard.

41
00:04:40,550 --> 00:04:44,070
and you will be speaking to me with more respect.

42
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:47,010
Kill the Braavosi. Bring the girl.

43
00:04:48,150 --> 00:04:50,960
Arya child, we are done with dancing for the day.

44
00:04:51,530 --> 00:04:53,000
Run to your father.

45
00:05:14,190 --> 00:05:15,770
Bloody oafs.

46
00:05:17,310 --> 00:05:18,710
Be gone now, Arya.

47
00:05:18,850 --> 00:05:21,500
Come with me. Run.

48
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:25,780
The first sword of Braavos does not run.

49
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:41,400
What do we say to the god of death?

50
00:05:42,640 --> 00:05:43,640
Not today.

51
00:05:45,820 --> 00:05:46,980
Go.

52
00:06:12,180 --> 00:06:14,460
Not today. Not today.

53
00:06:23,970 --> 00:06:25,220
Stay away from me.

54
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:27,870
I'll tell my father.

55
00:06:28,130 --> 00:06:30,850
I'll... I'll tell the queen.

56
00:06:32,090 --> 00:06:34,250
Who do you think sent me?

57
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:47,940
Needle.

58
00:06:51,790 --> 00:06:53,020
There she is.

59
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:56,220
- What do you want? - I want you, wolf girl.

60
00:06:56,230 --> 00:06:57,850
- Come here. - Leave me be.

61
00:06:57,860 --> 00:06:59,790
My father's a lord. He'll reward you.

62
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:01,550
She'll reward me... the queen!

63
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:03,740
Stay away!

64
00:07:32,980 --> 00:07:36,030
Lord Stark, you must be thirsty.

65
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:39,850
Varys.

66
00:07:42,060 --> 00:07:43,810
I promise you it isn't poisoned.

67
00:07:45,760 --> 00:07:47,980
Why is it no one ever trusts the eunuch?

68
00:07:56,750 --> 00:07:58,480
Not so much, my lord.

69
00:07:58,830 --> 00:08:00,610
I would save the rest, if I were you.

70
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:04,480
Hide it. Men have been known to die of thirst in these cells.

71
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:07,730
What about my daughters?

72
00:08:08,790 --> 00:08:11,130
The younger one seems to have escaped the castle.

73
00:08:11,310 --> 00:08:13,750
Even my little birds cannot find her.

74
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:17,020
- And Sansa? - Still engaged to Joffrey.

75
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:18,880
Cersei will keep her close.

76
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:22,150
The rest of your household though... all dead,

77
00:08:22,150 --> 00:08:23,490
it grieves me to say.

78
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:25,220
I do so hate the sight of blood.

79
00:08:26,660 --> 00:08:29,510
You watched my men being slaughtered and did nothing.

80
00:08:29,820 --> 00:08:31,840
And would again, my lord.

81
00:08:32,260 --> 00:08:33,980
I was unarmed, unarmored

82
00:08:33,980 --> 00:08:36,270
and surrounded by Lannister swords.

83
00:08:36,650 --> 00:08:38,900
When you look at me do you see a hero?

84
00:08:45,040 --> 00:08:47,280
What madness led you to tell the queen

85
00:08:47,290 --> 00:08:50,000
you had learned the truth about Joffrey's birth?

86
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,850
The madness of mercy.

87
00:08:56,950 --> 00:08:58,590
That she might save her children.

88
00:08:58,920 --> 00:09:00,780
Ah, the children.

89
00:09:00,780 --> 00:09:02,610
It is always the innocents who suffer.

90
00:09:04,030 --> 00:09:06,690
It wasn't the wine that killed Robert, nor the boar.

91
00:09:07,170 --> 00:09:10,000
The wine slowed him down and the boar ripped him open,

92
00:09:10,610 --> 00:09:13,510
But it was your mercy that killed the king.

93
00:09:17,190 --> 00:09:19,970
I trust you know you are a dead man, Lord Eddard?

94
00:09:25,070 --> 00:09:26,300
The queen can't kill me.

95
00:09:27,530 --> 00:09:28,680
Cat holds her brother.

96
00:09:29,810 --> 00:09:32,030
The wrong brother sadly.

97
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:33,930
And lost to her.

98
00:09:34,420 --> 00:09:37,280
Your wife has let the Imp slip through her fingers.

99
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:42,410
If that's true,

100
00:09:44,820 --> 00:09:46,680
then slit my throat and be done with it.

101
00:09:48,010 --> 00:09:49,440
Not today, my lord.

102
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:54,620
Tell me something, Varys.

103
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:58,310
Who do you truly serve?

104
00:09:59,990 --> 00:10:01,690
The realm, my lord.

105
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:04,000
Someone must.

106
00:10:23,640 --> 00:10:26,310
It's Othor, without a doubt.

107
00:10:27,610 --> 00:10:29,270
The other one is Jafer Flowers, my lord,

108
00:10:29,640 --> 00:10:31,550
Less the hand the wolf tore off.

109
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:34,950
Any sign of Benjen or the rest of his party?

110
00:10:35,850 --> 00:10:37,070
Just these two, my lord.

111
00:10:38,070 --> 00:10:39,330
Been dead awhile, I'd say.

112
00:10:39,880 --> 00:10:42,630
The smell.

113
00:10:46,170 --> 00:10:46,950
What smell?

114
00:10:48,950 --> 00:10:49,750
There is none.

115
00:10:50,810 --> 00:10:53,400
If they'd be dead for a long time, wouldn't there be rot?

116
00:10:55,940 --> 00:10:56,910
We should burn them.

117
00:10:57,230 --> 00:11:00,110
Snow's not wrong, my lord. Fire will do for them.

118
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:01,860
The wildling way.

119
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:05,270
I want Maester Aemon to examine them first.

120
00:11:06,490 --> 00:11:08,140
You may be a coward, Tarly,

121
00:11:08,430 --> 00:11:09,550
but you're not stupid.

122
00:11:11,250 --> 00:11:14,390
- Get them inside. - You heard him.

123
00:11:16,020 --> 00:11:16,980
Lord Commander,

124
00:11:18,980 --> 00:11:21,600
Maester Aemon awaits you in his chambers...

125
00:11:21,920 --> 00:11:24,390
A raven from King's Landing.

126
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:26,350
Come on, move 'em out.

127
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:40,490
Bring me a horn of ale, Snow,

128
00:11:41,670 --> 00:11:43,290
and pour one for yourself.

129
00:11:53,840 --> 00:11:55,920
The king is dead.

130
00:12:08,780 --> 00:12:10,260
Is there any word of my father?

131
00:12:11,060 --> 00:12:11,840
Sit.

132
00:12:18,170 --> 00:12:21,910
Lord Stark has been charged with treason.

133
00:12:23,270 --> 00:12:25,490
They say he conspired with Robert's brothers

134
00:12:26,180 --> 00:12:28,290
to deny the throne to Prince Joffrey.

135
00:12:40,910 --> 00:12:43,790
I hope you're not thinking of doing anything stupid.

136
00:12:44,590 --> 00:12:47,740
Your duty lies here now.

137
00:12:48,300 --> 00:12:50,190
My sisters were in King's Landing too.

138
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:54,810
I'm sure they'll be

139
00:12:55,550 --> 00:12:57,300
treated gently.

140
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:04,130
Your father has proved to be an awful traitor, dear.

141
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:07,100
King Robert's body was still warm

142
00:13:07,210 --> 00:13:08,520
when Lord Eddard began

143
00:13:08,530 --> 00:13:11,800
plotting to steal Joffrey's rightful throne.

144
00:13:12,290 --> 00:13:13,860
He wouldn't do that.

145
00:13:13,930 --> 00:13:16,800
He knows how much I love Joffrey. He wouldn't.

146
00:13:17,670 --> 00:13:19,720
Please, your grace, there's been a mistake.

147
00:13:19,730 --> 00:13:21,510
Send for my father. He'll tell you...

148
00:13:21,510 --> 00:13:23,370
the king was his friend.

149
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:26,780
Sansa sweetling, you are innocent of any wrong. We know that.

150
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:29,210
Yet you are the daughter of a traitor.

151
00:13:30,110 --> 00:13:32,210
How can I allow you to marry my son?

152
00:13:33,030 --> 00:13:35,660
A child born of a traitor's seed

153
00:13:35,670 --> 00:13:38,050
is no fit consort for our king.

154
00:13:38,190 --> 00:13:40,410
She is a sweet thing now, your grace,

155
00:13:40,570 --> 00:13:42,630
but in 10 years who knows

156
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:44,560
what treasons she may hatch?

157
00:13:45,140 --> 00:13:48,370
No, I'm not. I'll be a good wife to him, you'll see.

158
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:50,600
I'll be a queen just like you, I promise.

159
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:52,670
I won't hatch anything.

160
00:13:53,950 --> 00:13:56,870
The girl is innocent, your grace.

161
00:13:57,080 --> 00:13:59,960
She should be given a chance to prove her loyalty.

162
00:14:06,820 --> 00:14:09,640
Little dove, you must write to Lady Catelyn

163
00:14:10,130 --> 00:14:11,950
and your brother, the eldest, what's his name?

164
00:14:12,570 --> 00:14:13,370
Robb.

165
00:14:13,800 --> 00:14:16,940
Word of your father's arrest will reach him soon, no doubt.

166
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:18,330
Best it comes from you.

167
00:14:19,300 --> 00:14:20,800
If you would help your father,

168
00:14:21,330 --> 00:14:23,530
urge your brother to keep the king's peace.

169
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:25,680
Tell him to come to King's Landing

170
00:14:25,690 --> 00:14:27,580
and swear his fealty to Joffrey.

171
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:37,120
If... if I could see my father, talk to him about...

172
00:14:40,150 --> 00:14:41,520
You disappoint me, child.

173
00:14:43,660 --> 00:14:45,710
We have told you of your father's treason.

174
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:47,700
Why would you want to speak to a traitor?

175
00:14:48,920 --> 00:14:50,130
I only meant that...

176
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:54,110
What will happen to him?

177
00:14:55,970 --> 00:15:00,010
- That depends. - On... on what?

178
00:15:00,020 --> 00:15:01,040
On your brother.

179
00:15:04,980 --> 00:15:05,930
And on you.

180
00:15:15,260 --> 00:15:16,400
Treason?

181
00:15:18,350 --> 00:15:19,620
Sansa wrote this?

182
00:15:19,630 --> 00:15:22,490
It is your sister's hand, but the queen's words.

183
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:23,860
You are summoned to King's Landing

184
00:15:23,870 --> 00:15:25,990
to swear fealty to the new king.

185
00:15:26,590 --> 00:15:30,250
Joffrey puts my father in chains, now he wants his ass kissed?

186
00:15:30,740 --> 00:15:33,070
This is a royal command, my lord.

187
00:15:33,490 --> 00:15:36,280
- If you should refuse to obey... - I won't refuse.

188
00:15:37,340 --> 00:15:38,950
His grace summons me to King's Landing,

189
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:40,660
I'll go to King's Landing.

190
00:15:42,790 --> 00:15:43,900
But not alone.

191
00:15:46,690 --> 00:15:47,760
Call the banners.

192
00:15:50,380 --> 00:15:51,800
All of them, my lord?

193
00:15:51,940 --> 00:15:53,820
They've all sworn to defend my father, have they not?

194
00:15:53,820 --> 00:15:55,250
They have.

195
00:15:56,150 --> 00:15:57,840
Now we see what their words are worth.

196
00:16:09,820 --> 00:16:10,820
Are you afraid?

197
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:15,920
I must be.

198
00:16:16,860 --> 00:16:17,690
Good.

199
00:16:19,300 --> 00:16:20,410
Why is that good?

200
00:16:21,050 --> 00:16:22,610
It means you're not stupid.

201
00:16:46,350 --> 00:16:48,260
You've had this since dawn?

202
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:51,960
He sent it to me, not you.

203
00:16:52,640 --> 00:16:54,530
I've only shown it to you as a courtesy.

204
00:16:54,540 --> 00:16:55,570
A courtesy?!

205
00:16:56,100 --> 00:16:58,300
My husband has been taken prisoner.

206
00:16:58,330 --> 00:17:00,450
My son intends to declare war.

207
00:17:00,460 --> 00:17:01,320
A war?

208
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:04,250
Your son against the Lannisters?

209
00:17:05,510 --> 00:17:09,000
You should go to him. Teach him patience.

210
00:17:09,010 --> 00:17:12,500
Ned rots in a dungeon and you speak of patience?

211
00:17:12,650 --> 00:17:14,300
He is your brother by law!

212
00:17:14,720 --> 00:17:17,080
Does family mean nothing to you?

213
00:17:17,900 --> 00:17:20,000
Family means everything to me.

214
00:17:20,750 --> 00:17:22,610
And I will not risk Robin's life

215
00:17:22,620 --> 00:17:25,480
to get caught up in another of your husband's wars.

216
00:17:25,510 --> 00:17:28,470
- I'm hungry. - Hush now, darling.

217
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:30,230
You just ate.

218
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:32,370
You will not support us then?

219
00:17:32,370 --> 00:17:33,700
Do I understand you correctly?

220
00:17:33,710 --> 00:17:37,070
- But I'm hungry! - Soon, love, soon.

221
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:41,370
You're always welcome here, sister.

222
00:17:41,980 --> 00:17:44,690
But if you're asking me to send men from the Vale to fight...

223
00:17:44,700 --> 00:17:46,250
That is what I ask.

224
00:17:49,030 --> 00:17:52,230
Go on, sweet. Time for your bath.

225
00:17:53,290 --> 00:17:54,310
I'll feed you after.

226
00:17:59,900 --> 00:18:02,240
If you fear for the safety of your son...

227
00:18:02,250 --> 00:18:05,060
Of course I fear for the safety of my son!

228
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:06,920
Are you an idiot?

229
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:09,680
They killed my husband.

230
00:18:09,840 --> 00:18:12,210
You say they shoved your boy from a window.

231
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:14,890
These people will do anything.

232
00:18:14,900 --> 00:18:16,970
And that is why we have to stop them.

233
00:18:21,030 --> 00:18:25,210
The knights of the Vale will stay in the Vale where they belong,

234
00:18:25,210 --> 00:18:27,600
to protect their lord.

235
00:18:41,020 --> 00:18:42,200
Will you shut up?

236
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:47,750
There's hill tribes all around here.

237
00:18:49,100 --> 00:18:50,320
If I'm going to die,

238
00:18:50,660 --> 00:18:52,940
it may as well be with a song in my heart.

239
00:18:54,050 --> 00:18:56,120
I should just take your food and leave you here.

240
00:18:58,260 --> 00:18:59,570
What would you do then?

241
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,540
Starve, most likely.

242
00:19:02,430 --> 00:19:03,880
You don't think I'd do it, do you?

243
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:08,990
What do you want, Bronn? Gold? Women?

244
00:19:09,870 --> 00:19:11,060
Golden women?

245
00:19:11,850 --> 00:19:13,470
Stick with me and you'll have them all,

246
00:19:14,270 --> 00:19:16,920
for as long as I'm around and not for a moment longer.

247
00:19:18,250 --> 00:19:19,400
But you knew that.

248
00:19:20,390 --> 00:19:23,860
That is why you so valiantly took up arms to defend my honor.

249
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:26,860
Fair enough.

250
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:30,630
But don't go looking for me to bend the knee

251
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:33,250
and "My lord" you every time you take a shit.

252
00:19:34,060 --> 00:19:36,720
I'm not your toady and I'm not your friend.

253
00:19:37,640 --> 00:19:39,410
Though I would treasure your friendship,

254
00:19:40,030 --> 00:19:42,290
I'm mainly interested in your facility with murder.

255
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:46,150
And if the day ever comes when you're tempted to sell me out,

256
00:19:46,160 --> 00:19:47,190
remember this:

257
00:19:47,670 --> 00:19:50,650
whatever their price, I'll beat it.

258
00:19:51,140 --> 00:19:52,260
I like living.

259
00:19:59,750 --> 00:20:00,760
Tyrion.

260
00:20:02,790 --> 00:20:03,670
Tyrion.

261
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:09,460
Tyrion.

262
00:20:32,050 --> 00:20:33,740
Come, share our fire.

263
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:36,880
Help yourselves to our goat.

264
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:46,280
When you meet your gods, you tell them

265
00:20:46,290 --> 00:20:48,860
Shagga son of Dolf

266
00:20:48,870 --> 00:20:51,070
of the Stone Crows sent you.

267
00:20:52,150 --> 00:20:55,310
I am Tyrion son of Tywin of Clan Lannister.

268
00:20:55,320 --> 00:20:58,250
How would you like to die, Tyrion son of Tywin?

269
00:21:00,310 --> 00:21:02,790
In my own bed, at the age of 80

270
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:06,220
with a bellyful of wine and a girl's mouth around my cock.

