539
00:46:10,670 --> 00:46:12,780
to imprison his dear friend Ned?

540
00:46:12,790 --> 00:46:14,840
Robert Baratheon is dead.

541
00:46:14,840 --> 00:46:17,460
Joffrey rules in King's Landing.

542
00:46:19,680 --> 00:46:21,950
My sister rules, you mean.

543
00:46:22,140 --> 00:46:24,730
Stark's son has called his banners.

544
00:46:24,730 --> 00:46:28,730
- He moves south with a strong host. - A green boy.

545
00:46:28,780 --> 00:46:31,640
One taste of battle and he'll run back to Winterfell

546
00:46:31,640 --> 00:46:33,110
with his tail between his legs.

547
00:46:33,940 --> 00:46:35,290
Maybe.

548
00:46:35,450 --> 00:46:38,400
Though the boy does have a certain belligerence.

549
00:46:38,470 --> 00:46:40,090
You'd like him.

550
00:46:41,200 --> 00:46:45,220
While we're on the subject of war,

551
00:46:45,320 --> 00:46:47,850
I made promises to my friends here

552
00:46:47,850 --> 00:46:50,090
and a Lannister always pays his debts.

553
00:46:50,090 --> 00:46:53,050
We shall require 3,000 helms and shields,

554
00:46:53,050 --> 00:46:55,280
plus swords, pikes,

555
00:46:55,280 --> 00:46:57,090
gorgets, maces...

556
00:46:57,970 --> 00:46:59,490
If it please my lord,

557
00:46:59,490 --> 00:47:00,790
Ser Addam bids me report that

558
00:47:00,790 --> 00:47:03,580
the northmen have crossed the Neck.

559
00:47:05,210 --> 00:47:07,670
The wolf rushes into the lion's jaws.

560
00:47:07,670 --> 00:47:12,120
So be it. Kevan, command the drummers beat assembly.

561
00:47:13,670 --> 00:47:14,760
And send word to Jaime

562
00:47:14,760 --> 00:47:16,800
that I am moving against Robb Stark.

563
00:47:16,800 --> 00:47:18,230
At once, my lord.

564
00:47:31,410 --> 00:47:34,590
It is said that the men of the mountain clans are great warriors.

565
00:47:34,590 --> 00:47:36,190
Ride with me against my enemies

566
00:47:36,190 --> 00:47:39,340
and you shall have all my son promised you and more.

567
00:47:39,340 --> 00:47:42,140
Only if the half man fights with us.

568
00:47:42,140 --> 00:47:44,930
Until we hold the steel he pledged us,

569
00:47:44,970 --> 00:47:47,760
the little lion's life is ours.

570
00:47:53,210 --> 00:47:56,040
The scouts report Lord Tywin moves north.

571
00:47:56,050 --> 00:47:57,650
We need to get him on broken ground,

572
00:47:57,650 --> 00:47:59,260
put his knights at a disadvantage.

573
00:47:59,260 --> 00:48:01,270
No, we need to get around him

574
00:48:01,270 --> 00:48:04,550
and break Jaime Lannister's siege of Riverrun.

575
00:48:04,550 --> 00:48:07,380
Do that and the River Lords will join us.

576
00:48:07,380 --> 00:48:09,510
To do either we need to cross the river

577
00:48:09,510 --> 00:48:11,270
and the only crossing is at the Twins.

578
00:48:11,270 --> 00:48:13,090
Lord Frey controls that bridge.

579
00:48:13,090 --> 00:48:14,740
Your father's bannerman.

580
00:48:14,940 --> 00:48:18,100
"The late Lord Frey" My father calls him.

581
00:48:18,100 --> 00:48:21,440
At the Trident, he didn't appear until the battle was done.

582
00:48:21,800 --> 00:48:25,490
Some men takes their oaths more seriously than others.

583
00:48:32,880 --> 00:48:35,590
Robb's right. We need that bridge.

584
00:48:35,590 --> 00:48:37,430
So what's it going to be?

585
00:48:37,730 --> 00:48:41,550
Do we move against Jaime or lord Tywin?

586
00:48:45,790 --> 00:48:47,540
Your pardon, my lords.

587
00:48:47,540 --> 00:48:49,770
We've captured a Lannister scout.

588
00:48:51,270 --> 00:48:55,360
Don't worry, lad. He won't be leaving this tent with his head.

589
00:48:56,320 --> 00:48:58,010
Where did you find him?

590
00:48:58,010 --> 00:49:00,090
In the brush above the encampment.

591
00:49:00,090 --> 00:49:01,820
He looked to be counting.

592
00:49:12,730 --> 00:49:14,400
How high did you get?

593
00:49:16,590 --> 00:49:18,300
20,000. Maybe more.

594
00:49:19,770 --> 00:49:21,600
You don't have to do this yourself.

595
00:49:21,890 --> 00:49:22,970
Your father would understand...

596
00:49:22,970 --> 00:49:26,550
My father unrstands mercy, when there is room for it.

597
00:49:28,720 --> 00:49:30,480
And he understands honor...

598
00:49:32,870 --> 00:49:34,170
and courage.

599
00:49:37,190 --> 00:49:38,670
Let him go.

600
00:49:40,110 --> 00:49:41,260
Robb.

601
00:49:54,470 --> 00:49:57,890
Tell lord Tywin winter is coming for him.

602
00:49:57,890 --> 00:50:00,200
20,000 northerners marching south

603
00:50:00,200 --> 00:50:02,800
to find out if he really does shit gold.

604
00:50:04,260 --> 00:50:05,680
Yes, my lord.

605
00:50:06,640 --> 00:50:08,300
Thank you, my lord.

606
00:50:17,340 --> 00:50:21,080
Are you touched, boy?! Letting him go?

607
00:50:21,080 --> 00:50:22,980
You call me boy again.

608
00:50:24,520 --> 00:50:25,980
Go on.

609
00:50:51,490 --> 00:50:54,320
It is also the wish of his grace

610
00:50:54,580 --> 00:50:58,820
that his loyal servant Janos Slynt,

611
00:50:59,280 --> 00:51:02,290
- Commander of the city watch... - Ser Aron.

612
00:51:02,310 --> 00:51:06,690
be at once raised to the rank of lord...

613
00:51:07,060 --> 00:51:11,720
- Lord Gyles. - ...And granted the ancient seat of Harrenhal,

614
00:51:11,730 --> 00:51:15,490
and that his sons and grandsons shall hold this honor

615
00:51:15,490 --> 00:51:20,490
after him until the end of time.

616
00:51:24,030 --> 00:51:28,210
In the place of the traitor Eddard Stark,

617
00:51:28,210 --> 00:51:32,780
it is the wish of his grace that Tywin Lannister,

618
00:51:32,780 --> 00:51:36,770
Lord of Casterly Rock and Warden of the West,

619
00:51:36,770 --> 00:51:40,020
be appointed Hand of the king.

620
00:51:40,400 --> 00:51:45,400
Lastly, in these times of treason and turmoil,

621
00:51:45,620 --> 00:51:48,310
it is the view of the council

622
00:51:48,310 --> 00:51:51,530
that the life and safety

623
00:51:51,660 --> 00:51:53,760
of King Joffrey

624
00:51:53,760 --> 00:51:58,120
be of paramount importance.

625
00:51:59,520 --> 00:52:01,720
Ser Barristan Selmy.

626
00:52:08,510 --> 00:52:11,820
Your grace, I am yours to command.

627
00:52:11,820 --> 00:52:13,550
Rise, ser Barristan.

628
00:52:14,970 --> 00:52:16,980
You may remove your helm.

629
00:52:22,200 --> 00:52:24,810
You have served the realm long and faithfully.

630
00:52:24,810 --> 00:52:28,390
Every man and woman in the Seven Kingdoms owes you thanks.

631
00:52:28,520 --> 00:52:31,890
But it is time to put aside your armor and your sword.

632
00:52:32,210 --> 00:52:35,030
It is time to rest and look back with pride

633
00:52:35,030 --> 00:52:37,070
on your many years of service.

634
00:52:39,130 --> 00:52:41,640
Your grace, the kingsguard is a sworn brotherhood.

635
00:52:41,640 --> 00:52:43,460
Our vows are taken for life.

636
00:52:43,460 --> 00:52:46,250
Only death relieves us of our sacred trust.

637
00:52:46,260 --> 00:52:50,360
Whose death, ser Barristan? Yours or your king's?

638
00:52:50,780 --> 00:52:52,910
You let my father die.

639
00:52:52,910 --> 00:52:56,190
You're too old to protect anybody.

640
00:52:58,350 --> 00:53:00,800
- Your grace... - The council has determined

641
00:53:00,800 --> 00:53:03,330
that ser Jaime Lannister will take your place

642
00:53:03,330 --> 00:53:05,860
as lord commander of the kingsguard.

643
00:53:05,860 --> 00:53:07,230
The man who profaned his blade

644
00:53:07,240 --> 00:53:09,140
with the blood of the king he had sworn to defend!

645
00:53:09,140 --> 00:53:10,580
Careful, Ser.

646
00:53:11,250 --> 00:53:12,850
We have nothing but gratitude

647
00:53:12,850 --> 00:53:15,180
for your long service, good ser.

648
00:53:15,180 --> 00:53:18,300
You shall be given a stout keep beside the sea,

649
00:53:18,300 --> 00:53:20,950
with servants to look after your every need.

650
00:53:20,950 --> 00:53:23,080
A hall to die in

651
00:53:23,090 --> 00:53:25,270
and men to bury me.

652
00:53:27,130 --> 00:53:28,730
I am a knight.

653
00:53:29,560 --> 00:53:32,680
I shall die a knight.

654
00:53:38,370 --> 00:53:41,080
A naked knight, apparently.

655
00:53:51,750 --> 00:53:55,610
Even now I could cut through the five of you like carving a cake!

656
00:53:59,760 --> 00:54:00,990
Here, boy!

657
00:54:01,860 --> 00:54:04,550
Melt it down and add it to the others.

658
00:54:21,300 --> 00:54:23,500
If any man in this hall has other matters

659
00:54:23,500 --> 00:54:26,980
to set before his grace, let him speak now

660
00:54:27,220 --> 00:54:29,850
or go forth and hold his silence.

661
00:54:32,990 --> 00:54:34,500
Your grace.

662
00:54:35,930 --> 00:54:37,550
Come forward, my lady.

663
00:54:38,890 --> 00:54:41,270
The lady Sansa of house Stark.

664
00:54:42,950 --> 00:54:46,470
Do you have some business for the king and the council, Sansa?

665
00:54:46,930 --> 00:54:48,270
I do.

666
00:54:53,330 --> 00:54:56,680
As it please your grace, I ask mercy for my father,

667
00:54:56,970 --> 00:54:59,720
Lord Eddard Stark, who was Hand of the king.

668
00:54:59,720 --> 00:55:03,370
Treason is a noxious weed.

669
00:55:03,380 --> 00:55:07,230
- It should be torn out, root... - Let her speak.

670
00:55:07,490 --> 00:55:09,440
I want to hear what she says.

671
00:55:09,920 --> 00:55:11,710
Thank you, your grace.

672
00:55:11,990 --> 00:55:14,300
Do you deny your father's crime?

673
00:55:14,480 --> 00:55:18,470
No, my lords. I know he must be punished.

674
00:55:19,240 --> 00:55:21,180
All I ask is mercy.

675
00:55:21,480 --> 00:55:24,020
I know my lord father must regret what he did.

676
00:55:24,030 --> 00:55:26,030
He was King Robert's friend and he loved him.

677
00:55:26,030 --> 00:55:28,250
You all know he loved him.

678
00:55:28,470 --> 00:55:32,370
He never wanted to be Hand until the king asked him.

679
00:55:32,590 --> 00:55:35,560
They must have lied to him... lord Renly or lord Stannis

680
00:55:35,560 --> 00:55:38,280
or somebody. They must have lied!

681
00:55:38,770 --> 00:55:40,540
He said I wasn't the king.

682
00:55:41,740 --> 00:55:43,320
Why did he say that?

683
00:55:43,380 --> 00:55:45,270
He was badly hurt.

684
00:55:45,270 --> 00:55:48,410
Maester Pycelle was giving him milk of the poppy.

685
00:55:48,450 --> 00:55:52,280
He wasn't himself. Otherwise he never would have said it.

686
00:55:54,250 --> 00:55:59,080
A child's faith... Such sweet innocence.

687
00:55:59,280 --> 00:56:01,980
And yet they say wisdom oft comes

688
00:56:01,980 --> 00:56:04,040
from the mouths of babes.

689
00:56:04,060 --> 00:56:08,560
Treason is treason!

690
00:56:12,000 --> 00:56:13,610
Anything else?

691
00:56:15,040 --> 00:56:18,940
If you still have any affection in your heart for me,

692
00:56:18,940 --> 00:56:22,580
please do me this kindness, your grace.

693
00:56:32,030 --> 00:56:34,010
Your sweet words have moved me.

694
00:56:35,970 --> 00:56:38,070
But your father has to confess.

695
00:56:38,960 --> 00:56:42,930
He has to confess and say that I'm the king...

696
00:56:45,170 --> 00:56:47,250
or there'll be no mercy for him.

697
00:56:52,240 --> 00:56:53,580
He will.

